// 03 · Springs — a scarce nutrient, and a real carrying capacity.
//
// 02's meadow was capped only by space. Here a second, DECOUPLED axis enters
// (Liebig's law of the minimum): energy (sunlight) still governs SURVIVAL, but a
// scarce NUTRIENT now governs REPRODUCTION. A few vents (`sources`) leak the
// nutrient into a diffusing FIELD (toggle View ▸ Layers → Nutrient heatmap); a plant
// ABSORBS it into a small store and SPENDS it to seed (`repro_cost`) — and the spent
// nutrient is CONSUMED, not handed down, so it is a genuinely limiting resource.
// The vents supply it slowly, so seeding is nutrient-THROTTLED: the meadow grows far
// slower than 02's and stays pinned to the vents (nowhere else has nutrient to seed
// with). A dying plant RECYCLES its store back to the field (`emit_at_death`) —
// latent here (well-fed plants rarely die), it becomes the loop that carries the
// nutrient up the chain once a grazer starts killing them (04+). NB with immortal
// producers the nutrient bounds the growth RATE, not the standing crop; a firm
// carrying capacity needs turnover — which arrives with grazing.
//
// Watch: plants cluster into tight OASES around the three vents; the rest stays bare.
